course: dictionary
lesson: 5967
title: Words from the bedroom
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A mattress is the large, thick, soft pad you lie on in a bed. You can often work out a new word from the things around it. Words like bed, sleep and soft are clues that point to the meaning.
explain: «Money in a bank is protected up to a large limit in many countries, even if the bank fails; money under a mattress can be stolen or burnt.» The words under a mattress show you where the money is kept. A mattress is something a person can put things under, so it is thick and it lies on top of a bed.
explain: Some words gain a new meaning with another word in front. An air mattress is a plastic one you fill with air, for camping or for floating on water. The word air tells you how it works. Check your meaning by putting it into a sentence: "We slept on an air mattress in the tent" still makes sense.
fact: A mattress is a large, thick, soft pad that you lie on in a bed.
fact: An air mattress is a plastic mattress that you fill with air, for camping or for floating on water.
fact: «Mattress» is a noun, and its plural is «mattresses».
fact: In science lessons, a mattress is an example of a soft material and of springs.
fact: Mattresses must not be put near heaters, and babies should sleep on a firm mattress.
exercise: What is a mattress? | A blanket for cold nights | A plastic boat for the sea | *A large, thick, soft pad you lie on in a bed | A small pillow for your head
exercise: Mia says, «The tent is ready and the air mattress is in the bag.» What kind of mattress is it? | A thick spring mattress for a house | *A plastic one you fill with air, for camping | A wooden bench | A soft cushion for a chair
exercise: «Please carry the mattresses up the stairs.» Find and copy the plural word for mattress. | please | *mattresses | stairs | carry
test: Safety lessons say mattresses must not be put near heaters. Why? | Because heaters like soft things to sleep on | Because a heater makes the room too cold | *Because a heater could make them catch fire | Because mattresses are made of water
test: What does «spring mattress» suggest? | A mattress that jumps about | *A mattress with springs inside it | A mattress for the sea | A mattress made of water
exam: The sentence «money under a mattress can be stolen or burnt» suggests what about a mattress? | It is a loud musical instrument | It is a plastic toy boat | It is a kind of food | *It is a place where someone could hide things
